{
 "_doc": "Sentinel fallback + late-binding calibration corpus. Each case pins exact sequences through one hermetic op and the genuine causes of every fallback step. Ops: ladder (first_accept_in_order over scripted rungs; rung behavior serve:X | miss | err-terminal:MSG | err-continue:MSG; stop aborts only on err-terminal), expand (expand_group_keys over a fixture group; recency values are key:MEMBER (resolved to that member's wire id) or wire:LITERAL; loaded lists base keys reported running), climb (TargetMatcher over expanded candidates with per-candidate assess scripts err | N:reason | raw:TEXT), latebind (a live resolver table read per resolve; rewrite mutates the table between resolves), prefilter (deterministic filter match with a counting backend that must stay at zero calls), oneshot (instance-profile flag baseline). A fallback event is any step past a candidate with a recorded cause: rung transition after miss/err-continue, last-miss skip (no-record | removed-member), unloaded member ranked behind a loaded one, assess-err escalation, endpoint-rewrite, load-after-miss. A genuine failure is any injected availability gap (backend err/miss, missing/removed record, unloaded member in output, assess err, resolve miss); it must be followed (walk continues or cleanly exhausts). Controls must show zero fallback events with exact sequences. Precision = caused fallbacks / all fallbacks; recall = followed failures / all failures; control pass = controls clean / all controls. Nothing here enables caching, persistence, or traffic-shaping \u2014 measurement only.",
